      "content": "Here's an updated sample memo:\n\nDear Team,\n\nAs we continue to adapt to a remote work setup, we wanted to take a moment to remind everyone about the importance of maintaining a healthy and ergonomic workspace. Proper chair height and monitor placement are key to preventing neck strain, but what about hand and wrist comfort? When typing for extended periods, it's easy to develop bad habits that can lead to carpal tunnel syndrome or general hand discomfort. To avoid this, we recommend the following tips:\n\n* Keep your keyboard and mouse close to your body to avoid reaching and stretching\n* Place your keyboard directly in front of you, with your wrists straight and your elbows at a 90-degree angle\n* Take regular breaks (every 30-60 minutes) to stretch your hands, wrists, and arms\n* Consider using an ergonomic keyboard tray or wrist rest to reduce strain on your hands and wrists\n* Stop typing if you experience any pain or discomfort in your hands or wrists\n\nBy prioritizing your well-being and taking a few minutes to adjust your workspace, we're committed to supporting your overall health and happiness.",
